<Layouts.app flash={@flash} locale={@locale} path="/help">
  <article id="manual" class="manual">
    <h1>{gettext("Help")}</h1>

    <h2>{gettext("What Ascella does")}</h2>

    <p>
      {gettext(
        "Ascella installs, updates, starts and stops the hall's programs on this computer: OpenPairings, Alnasl, Arkab, Polis and Nunki. Each tile says what is installed, what is out, and whether it runs."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("Where the files come from")}</h2>

    <p>
      {gettext(
        "Only from each program's own releases on GitHub, over HTTPS. Every file is checked against the checksums the release publishes before it is used; a release without checksums is not installed, and a file that does not match is thrown away. Nothing that was not checked is ever started."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("Your data")}</h2>

    <p>
      {gettext(
        "An update replaces a program, never its data: tournaments, games and settings stay where they are. Ascella refuses any step that would touch a program's data folder, and says so on the tile."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("Updating")}</h2>

    <p>
      {gettext(
        "A program that is open is not updated: Ascella says so and offers to close it, because it may be in the middle of a round. Once it is closed, the update replaces the program and nothing else. If a program does not answer in time, Ascella gives up waiting, changes nothing more, and the tile says so. On a Mac the previous version is kept and the tile offers to go back to it, except for programs whose database changes on an update (OpenPairings and Alnasl): there is no way back for those."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("Per computer")}</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        {gettext(
          "Windows: the program's own installer for a first install, and its own updater (Velopack) after that. A copy installed for everyone, from the .msi, is left to the .msi."
        )}
      </li>

      <li>
        {gettext(
          "Mac: the app is downloaded, checked, unpacked and put in Applications in place of the old one. Because Ascella fetched it, the Mac does not block it as a download from the internet."
        )}
      </li>

      <li>
        {gettext(
          "Linux and Raspberry Pi: the program's own install and update scripts, and its own system service."
        )}
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>{gettext("Shortcuts")}</h2>

    <p>
      {gettext(
        "Once a program is installed, its tile offers to make it easy to start. Windows: a Start menu and a Desktop shortcut; to pin it to the taskbar, right-click the Start menu shortcut and choose Pin to taskbar (Windows offers no other way). Mac: keep it in the Dock, or open it at login. Linux: an entry in the applications menu, a file on the Desktop, and GNOME's favourites. Ascella writes down what it made and removes only that; a shortcut you made yourself is never touched. After an update the shortcuts are made again, so they never point at an old version."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("Removing a program")}</h2>

    <p>
      {gettext(
        "Remove on a tile stops the program, then removes it the way the computer does: its own uninstaller on Windows, the Bin on a Mac, its service and folder on Linux. The shortcuts Ascella made go with it. Its data (tournaments, games, settings) lives in separate folders and is kept; it is deleted only if you tick the box and then confirm a second time."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("Removing Ascella")}</h2>

    <p>
      <a id="remove-ascella-link" href={~p"/remove-ascella"}>
        {gettext("How to remove Ascella itself")}
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("Only this computer")}</h2>

    <p>
      {gettext(
        "This page answers this computer only, never the hall's network: whoever reaches it can install programs. On a box without a screen, use an SSH tunnel to port 4090."
      )}
    </p>

    <p id="help-key">
      {gettext(
        "On a Linux box where Ascella runs as a service, the page also wants a key that only root and the desktop user can read. Open it with: sh /opt/ascella/current/ascella.sh open (add --print to get the link instead, for example to paste in the browser at the other end of an SSH tunnel). Restarting Ascella makes a new key."
      )}
    </p>
  </article>
</Layouts.app>
